{"tool_name":"clinker","contents":["biotools","galaxy","oeb","bioschemas","biocontainers"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"clinker","identifiers":["doi:10.1093/gigascience/giy079"],"license":"MIT","summary":"Clinker is a bioinformatics pipeline that generates a supertranscriptome from popular fusion finder outputs (jaffa, tophatfusion, soap, defuse, pizzly, etc), that can be then be either viewed in genome viewers such as igv or through the included plotting feature developed with gviz.","home_url":"https://github.com/Oshlack/Clinker","keywords":["Alternative Splicing","Computational Biology","Frameshift Mutation","Gene Expression Profiling","Genomics","Humans","Leukemia, B-Cell","Oncogene Proteins, Fusion","Precursor Cell Lymphoblastic Leukemia-Lymphoma","Programming Languages","Protein Domains","Protein Isoforms","RNA","Receptors, Cytokine","Receptors, Purinergic P2Y","Sequence Analysis, RNA"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":341},"biotools":{"id":"clinker","home":"http://github.com/gamcil/clinker","license":"MIT","summary":"Automatic generation of gene cluster comparison figures.\n\nGene cluster comparison figure generator.\n\nA d3 chart for generating gene cluster comparison figures.\n\nclinker is a pipeline for easily generating publication-quality gene cluster comparison figures.\n\nGiven a set of GenBank files, clinker will automatically extract protein translations, perform global alignments between sequences in each cluster, determine the optimal display order based on cluster similarity, and generate an interactive visualisation (using clustermap.js) that can be extensively tweaked before being exported as an SVG file.\n\nclustermap.js is an interactive, reusable d3 chart designed to visualise homology between multiple gene clusters.","addition_date":"2021-01-18T11:45:41Z","last_update_date":"2021-02-12T15:37:21Z","biotools_curie":"biotools:clinker","edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Dendrogram visualisa